    "text_delta": "tself imply avoidance or unfairness.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\n\n1. **Send a professional follow-up to HR:**\n   Keep it warm and centered on professional growth. For example:\n   > *\"I am following up on my request from two weeks ago regarding feedback from my final interview for the Head of Clinical Laboratory position. I am very interested in understanding which areas or competencies I can strengthen as I continue to develop my leadership career within the hospital.\"*\n\n2. **Keep the focus on competencies, not panel demographics:**\n   Avoid mentioning the gender composition of the panel. Focus entirely on uncovering:\n   * How they scored strategic and operational leadership versus technical expertise.\n   * Specific areas where the panel felt the successful candidate had an edge.\n\n3. **Use the feedback to target future executive roles:**\n   If the feedback indicates they prioritized executive leadership over scientific credentials, consider highlighting broader hospital-wide initiatives, operational budgeting, or formal management credentials in your next application.\n",
